          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"}> dependent
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            and in particular in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are called (homotopy-)
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
          %blockquote
            %p
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#Rittri89"}> Rittri (1989)
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Cosmo95"} Cosmo (1995, §1.8)
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#HofmannStreicher98"} Hofmann &amp; Streicher (1998, §5.4)
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#KapulkinLumsdaine21"} Kapulkin &amp; Lumsdaine (2012, 2021, Def. 3.1.1)
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "#HistoricalNote"} below
          %p
            or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalent
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#UFP13"}> UFP13, §4
            \&amp;rbrack; (for fine-print see the definitions
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Definition"} below
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \to C
            which may be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverted
            (up to the relevant re-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identification+type"}> indentifications
            ), hence if any program operating on data of type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            may be transformed into a program operating on data of type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ApplicationsInProofReuse"} below
          %p
            Alternatively, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+type"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \to C
            may be called a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            if all its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-images"} pre-images
            are essentially unique, namely if all its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+types"} fiber types
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+types"} contractible types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            this is called a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            = succeed "&rbrack;." do
              %a{:href => "#Voevodsky10"} Voevodsky (2010), p. 8, 10
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/TypeEquivalence-230128b.jpg", :width => "800"}/
          %p
            These two notions are in fact equivalent &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#UFP13"}> UFP13, around Thm. 4.4.5
            \&amp;rbrack;.
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/TypeBijectionIsEquivalence-230128.jpg", :width => "750"}/
          %p
            In the special case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-truncated"} 0-truncated
            types (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-sets"}> h-sets
            ), hence in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theories"} dependent type theories
            with
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+K"} axiom K
            or the axiom imposing
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniqueness+of+identity+proofs"} uniqueness of identity proofs
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
            or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-to-one+correspondence"} one-to-one correspondence
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
          %p
            In the special case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-truncated"} 1-truncated
            types (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-groupoids"}> h-groupoids
            ), type equivalence corresponds essentially to the notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+groupoids"} equivalence of groupoids
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
          %p
            In full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of type equivalence is
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
            and that of type bijection is
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of types being as
            = succeed "-/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} co
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            coincide with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalences"} homotopy equivalences
            (by the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+theorem"} Whitehead theorem
          %p
            Finally, the notion of equivalence/bijection of types is
            %em a priori
            different from that of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identification+type"} identification
            of types in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
