          %h3#the_isequiv_type_family_and_equivalence_types The isEquiv type family and equivalence types
          %p#OutlookOnEquivalenceOfDefinitions
            As (eventually to be) discussed in the
            = succeed "-section" do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#Properties"} Properties
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+extensionality"} function extensionality
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-propositions"} h-propositions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+K"} axiom K
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniqueness+of+identity+proofs"} uniqueness of identity proofs
            (as discussed
            = succeed ");" do
              %a{:href => "#TheIssueWithQuasiInverses"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theories"} dependent type theories
            without either axiom, the isEquiv type family is not in general a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+proposition"} mere proposition
            for homotopy equivalences. However, often the most convenient way to show that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is an equivalence is by exhibiting it as a term of the type of homotopy equivalences.
          %h4#rules_for_isequiv Rules for isEquiv
          %p
            Given types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+types"} equivalence of types
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-inverse+function"} quasi-inverse function
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            satisfies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copy+type"} copy type
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            with copy function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-propositions"} h-propositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isEquiv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B \vdash \mathrm{isEquiv}(f)
            using very similar natural deduction rules to the rules for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copy+types"} copy types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/introduction+rule"} introduction rule
            states that given a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B
            and evidence that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            has a quasi-inverse function, one could form a witness of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isEquiv
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isEquiv}(f)
          %p Defining
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} qInv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo :
                        %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo ×
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A \to B \vdash \mathrm{qInv}(f) \equiv \sum_{g:B \to A} \left(\prod_{y:B} \mathrm{Id}_B(f(g(y)), y)\right) \times \left(\prod_{x:A} \mathrm{Id}_A(g(f(x)), x)\right)
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≡
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isProp}(A) \equiv \prod_{x:A} \prod_{y:A} x =_A y
          %p
            the formation and introduction rules for isEquiv state that that the type family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isEquiv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
