          %h2#Semantics Semantics
          %p
            We discuss the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of equivalences in homotopy type theory.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+category"} locally cartesian closed category
            which is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+factorization+system"} weak factorization system
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+path+objects"} stable path objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            could be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type-theoretic+model+category"} type-theoretic model category
          %h3#of_
            Of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi isEquiv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isEquiv(-)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B
              two
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+object"} cofibrant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A\to B
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
              or equivalently a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              precisely when the interpretation of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi isEquiv
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isEquiv(f)
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+element"} global point
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mi hasContrFibers
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * \to hasContrFibers(f)
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A\to B
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent type
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi hfiber
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    b\colon B
                    \\;\vdash\;
                    hfiber(f,b)\colon Type
            %p
              is by the rules for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} interpretation
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substitution"} substitution
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+path+space"} mapping path space
              construction
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P f
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi b
                            %mo :
                            %mi B
                            %mo ⊢
                            %mi hfiber
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo ,
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                            %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi B
                              %mi I
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    [b : B \vdash  hfiber(f,b)] &amp;\coloneqq &amp; P f  &amp;\to&amp; A
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; B^I &amp;\to&amp; B
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; B
                    }
            %p
              which, by the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+lemma"} factorization lemma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              as an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+cofibration"} acyclic cofibration
              followed by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi P
                    %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f : A \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} P f \to B
                    \\,.
            %p
              By definition and the semantics of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+types"} contractible types
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              are cofibrant, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi isEquiv
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} isEquiv(f)
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global element
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi b
                    %mi isContr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi hfiber
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    * \to \prod_{b} isContr(hfiber(f,b))
            %p
              precisely when in this factorization, the fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P f \to B
              is an acyclic fibration. (See for instance (
              %a{:href => "http://www.sandiego.edu/~shulman/hottminicourse2012/03models.pdf#page=49"}> Shulman, page 49
              ) for more details.)
            %p
              But by the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-3+property"} 2-out-of-3 property
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              being a weak equivalence — and hence a homotopy equivalence, since it is a map between fibrant-cofibrant objects.
          #InterpretationIfIsEquivAsDependentType.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In the above we fixed one function
