          %h2#References References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The notion of two-sided homotopy equivalence of types in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            appears (together with the formulation of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
          %ul
            %li#HofmannStreicher98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Hofmann"}> Martin Hofmann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Streicher"} Thomas Streicher
              = succeed "," do
                %em The groupoid interpretation of type theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Sambin"} Giovanni Sambin
              et al. (eds.),
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twenty-five years of constructive type theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 36
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/twenty-five-years-of-constructive-type-theory-9780198501275"} ISBN:9780198501275
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de/~streicher/venedig.ps.gz"} ps
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HofmannStreicherGroupoidInterpretation.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            except that these authors refer to the subtly incorrect type
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheSubtlyWrongTypeOfEquivalences"} (1)
            of all such equivalences.
          %p
            The notion of equivalences as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+type"} functions
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+type"} contractible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+type"} homotopy fibers
            (and thereby the fix of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence+axiom"} univalence axiom
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#HofmannStreicher98"} Hofmann &amp; Streicher (1998), §5.4
          %ul
            %li#Voevodsky10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Voevodsky"}> Vladimir Voevodsky
              , p. 10 of:
              %em Univalent Foundations Project
              (2010) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.ias.edu/~vladimir/Site3/Univalent_Foundations_files/univalent_foundations_project.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Voevodsky-UFP2010.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The notion of “homotopy isomorphisms” (functions with left- and right-quasi inverses) was proposed by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"} André Joyal
            in a 2011 Oberwolfach meeting, recorded in:
          %ul
            %li#KapulkinLumsdaine21
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Kapulkin"}> Chris Kapulkin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+LeFanu+Lumsdaine"} Peter LeFanu Lumsdaine
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Simplicial Model of Univalent Foundations (after Voevodsky)
              %strong 23
              (2021) 2071–2126 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1211.2851"}> arXiv:1211.2851
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4171/jems/1050"} doi:10.4171/jems/1050
          %p
            The notion of equivalences as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-to-one+correspondences"} one-to-one correspondences
            is due to:
          %ul
            %li#Shulman22
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              , Towards a Third-Generation HOTT Part 1 (
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/slides/shulman-2022-04-28.pdf"}> slides
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FrxkVzItMzA"} video
          %p Introduction and exposition:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"}> Andrej Bauer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em HoTT equivalences
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://math.andrej.com/2011/12/07/hott-equivalences/"} webpage
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V3YUsZx_fmo"} video
            %li#Shulman
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
                , from
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://home.sandiego.edu/~shulman/hottminicourse2012/02hott.pdf#page=60"} slide 60 of part 2
                %a{:href => "https://home.sandiego.edu/~shulman/hottminicourse2012/03models.pdf#page=49"} slide 49 of part 3
                in:
                %em Minicourse in homotopy type theory
                (2012) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://home.sandiego.edu/~shulman/hottminicourse2012/"}> web
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"}> Andrej Bauer
                ,
                %em Equivalences
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BuI62-o3Ds8"}> video
                \&amp;rbrack;, Part 4 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL-47DDuiZOMCRDiXDZ1fI0TFLQgQqOdDa"} Introduction to homotopy type theory
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li#UFP13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
              , §2.4 and §4 in:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+--+Univalent+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
              (2013) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://homotopytypetheory.org/book/"}> web
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://hottheory.files.wordpress.com/2013/03/hott-online-323-g28e4374.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Implementation of equivalences in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+assistants"} proof assistants
          %p
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "https://github.com/HoTT/HoTT/blob/master/theories/Basics/Equivalences.v"} github.com/HoTT/HoTT/blob/master/theories/Basics/Equivalences.v
          %p
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "https://agda.github.io/agda-stdlib/v1.1/Function.Equivalence.html"} agda.github.io/agda-stdlib/v1.1/Function.Equivalence.html
          %p On equivalences as one-to-one correspondences in homotopy type theory:
          %ul
            %li
              Mike Shulman,
              %em Towards a Third-Generation HOTT
              Part 1 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://www.cmu.edu/dietrich/philosophy/hott/slides/shulman-2022-04-28.pdf"}> slides
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FrxkVzItMzA"} video
          %h3#ApplicationsInProofReuse Applications
          %p
            Origin of the notion of type isomorphy in and application to
            = succeed "-theory" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/programming+language"} programming language
          %ul
            %li#Rittri89
              %p
                Mikael Rittri,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Using types as search keys in function libraries
                %em FPCA ‘89: Proceedings of the fourth international conference on Functional programming languages and computer architecture
                (1989) 174–183 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1145/99370.99384"}> doi:10.1145/99370.99384
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/99370.99384"} pdf
            %li#Cosmo95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roberto+Di+Cosmo"}> Roberto Di Cosmo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Isomorphisms of Types – from
                    = succeed "-calculus" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi λ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4612-2572-0"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4612-2572-0
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gilles+Barthe"}> Gilles Barthe
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Olivier+Pons"} Olivier Pons
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Type Isomorphisms and Proof Reuse in Dependent Type Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Foundations of Software Science and Computation Structures. FoSSaCS 2001
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 2030
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-45315-6_4"} doi:10.1007/3-540-45315-6_4
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roberto+Di+Cosmo"}> Roberto Di Cosmo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A short survey of isomorphisms of types
                %strong 15
                5 (2005) 825-838 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0960129505004871"}> doi:10.1017/S0960129505004871
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.dicosmo.org/Articles/mscs-survey.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Talia+Ringer"}> Talia Ringer
                , RanDair Porter, Nathaniel Yazdani, John Leo, Dan Grossman,
                %em Proof Repair across Type Equivalences
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.00774"}> arXiv:2010.00774
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Talia+Ringer"}> Talia Ringer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Proof repair along type equivalences
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Proof Repair
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.proquest.com/docview/2568297410"} proquest:2568297410
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_BkTrp44uBU"} video
